[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW-PATHS
TITLE: The paths that must work
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
STATEMENT: >>>
Three use cases, each covered by the rulings and programs it points at with Covered_By. Each is designed; none has yet been walked end to end against the built programs and recorded as evidence.

- The operator chooses a different word for a ruled term, and every narrative that used it shows a drifted citation. [LINK: UC-RENAME-A-TERM] [SETTLED]
- A ruling lands, the sections that cite it show drift, and only those are re-read, re-cut and re-signed. [LINK: UC-RECUT-AFTER-A-RULING] [SETTLED]
- The view renders its own design from this root through the same programs, with no renderer change. [LINK: UC-FLIP-THE-VIEW] [SETTLED]
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
UC-FLIP-THE-VIEW:0000000
UC-RECUT-AFTER-A-RULING:0000000
UC-RENAME-A-TERM:0000000
<<<
